+## Read-only replay catalog
+
+Use `spiral tui-replay-list` to inspect the replay cases selected by a TUI
+replay spec without executing any case:
+
+```console
+$ spiral tui-replay-list --tool-root . --filter observer --max-cases 1
+{"version":1,"total":1,"cases":[{"id":"pane-prefs-observer-suggestion","tags":["tui","observer","suggestion","prefs"]}]}
+```
+
+The default spec is `.spiral-coder/tui_replay.json`; `--spec` may name another
+spec and relative paths are resolved under `--tool-root` (also available as
+`-C`). Selection preserves spec order. `--filter` performs an ASCII
+case-insensitive substring match against each case id and tag, while
+`--max-cases` truncates after filtering; a zero cap is treated as one. Tags
+are returned in their original order. Empty selections and invalid cases are
+errors. Listing only reads and validates the spec: it does not run replay
+cases, invoke a provider, require credentials, or create artifacts. Use
+`spiral tui-replay` when you want to execute the selected cases and receive
+the normal replay report instead.
+
